+ '<div class="think-box"><strong>Think about it:</strong> Why should you never write bare <code>except:</code> (without specifying a type)? Because it catches <em>everything</em>, including <code>SystemExit</code> (raised by <code>sys.exit()</code>) and <code>KeyboardInterrupt</code> (raised by Ctrl+C). If you catch those, your program becomes unkillable. At minimum, use <code>except Exception:</code> which skips those two. But even better: always catch the <em>specific</em> exception you expect.</div>'

/* ============================================================
   SECTION 5: LOGGING
   ============================================================ */
+ '<h2 class="l-title">5. Logging</h2>'

+ '<p class="l-text"><strong>Professional programs do not use print() for diagnostics.</strong> The <code>logging</code> module is Python\'s built-in solution for recording events during program execution. Unlike <code>print()</code>, logging lets you control <em>severity levels</em>, route messages to different <em>destinations</em> (console, files, network), add <em>timestamps and context</em> automatically, and enable/disable output without changing your code.</p>'

+ '<div class="calc-cards">'
+ '<div class="calc-card"><div class="cc-icon">D</div><div class="cc-title">DEBUG (10)</div><div class="cc-body">Detailed diagnostic info.<br>Only for development.<br><code>logging.debug(msg)</code></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-card"><div class="cc-icon">I</div><div class="cc-title">INFO (20)</div><div class="cc-body">General operational events.<br>"Server started on port 8080"<br><code>logging.info(msg)</code></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-card"><div class="cc-icon">W</div><div class="cc-title">WARNING (30)</div><div class="cc-body">Something unexpected but not fatal.<br>"Disk 85% full"<br><code>logging.warning(msg)</code></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-card"><div class="cc-icon">E</div><div class="cc-title">ERROR (40)</div><div class="cc-body">An operation failed.<br>"Failed to save user data"<br><code>logging.error(msg)</code></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-card"><div class="cc-icon">C</div><div class="cc-title">CRITICAL (50)</div><div class="cc-body">System is about to crash.<br>"Database connection lost"<br><code>logging.critical(msg)</code></div></div>'
+ '</div>'

+ '<div class="calc-compare"><div class="compare-col"><div class="compare-title">print() — BAD</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; No severity levels</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Goes to stdout only</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; No timestamps</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Cannot be disabled easily</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Mixes with program output</div></div><div class="compare-col"><div class="compare-title">logging — GOOD</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; 5 severity levels</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Multiple destinations</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Auto timestamps + context</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Level filtering built-in</div><div class="compare-item">&bull; Zero-cost when disabled</div></div></div>'

+ '<div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-label"><span>PYTHON</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest(\'.code-wrap\').querySelector(\'code\').textContent)">COPY</button></div><pre class="code-block"><code><span class="kw">import</span> logging\n\n<span class="cm"># Basic configuration — quick setup</span>\nlogging.<span class="fn">basicConfig</span>(\n    level=logging.DEBUG,\n    format=<span class="str">"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s: %(message)s"</span>,\n    datefmt=<span class="str">"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"</span>\n)\n\nlogger = logging.<span class="fn">getLogger</span>(<span class="str">"myapp"</span>)\n\nlogger.<span class="fn">debug</span>(<span class="str">"Connecting to database..."</span>)\nlogger.<span class="fn">info</span>(<span class="str">"User \'alice\' logged in"</span>)\nlogger.<span class="fn">warning</span>(<span class="str">"API rate limit at 80%"</span>)\nlogger.<span class="fn">error</span>(<span class="str">"Failed to fetch user profile: timeout"</span>)\nlogger.<span class="fn">critical</span>(<span class="str">"Database connection lost!"</span>)\n\n<span class="cm"># Output:</span>\n<span class="cm"># 2024-01-15 14:30:22 [DEBUG] myapp: Connecting to database...</span>\n<span class="cm"># 2024-01-15 14:30:22 [INFO] myapp: User \'alice\' logged in</span>\n<span class="cm"># ...</span></code></pre></div>'

+ '<p class="l-text"><strong>Professional logging setup</strong> — In real projects, you want different handlers for different destinations:</p>'

+ '<div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-label"><span>PSEUDOCODE</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest(\'.code-wrap\').querySelector(\'code\').textContent)">COPY</button></div><pre class="code-block"><code><span class="kw">import</span> logging\n<span class="kw">from</span> logging.handlers <span class="kw">import</span> RotatingFileHandler\n\n<span class="cm"># Create logger</span>\nlogger = logging.<span class="fn">getLogger</span>(<span class="str">"myapp"</span>)\nlogger.<span class="fn">setLevel</span>(logging.DEBUG)     <span class="cm"># capture everything</span>\n\n<span class="cm"># Console handler — show INFO and above</span>\nconsole = logging.<span class="fn">StreamHandler</span>()\nconsole.<span class="fn">setLevel</span>(logging.INFO)\nconsole.<span class="fn">setFormatter</span>(logging.<span class="fn">Formatter</span>(\n    <span class="str">"%(levelname)s: %(message)s"</span>\n))\n\n<span class="cm"># File handler — log everything, rotate at 5MB, keep 3 backups</span>\nfile_handler = <span class="fn">RotatingFileHandler</span>(\n    <span class="str">"app.log"</span>, maxBytes=<span class="num">5_000_000</span>, backupCount=<span class="num">3</span>\n)\nfile_handler.<span class="fn">setLevel</span>(logging.DEBUG)\nfile_handler.<span class="fn">setFormatter</span>(logging.<span class="fn">Formatter</span>(\n    <span class="str">"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s.%(funcName)s:%(lineno)d — %(message)s"</span>\n))\n\nlogger.<span class="fn">addHandler</span>(console)\nlogger.<span class="fn">addHandler</span>(file_handler)\n\n<span class="cm"># Usage with exception info</span>\n<span class="kw">try</span>:\n    result = risky_operation()\n<span class="kw">except</span> Exception:\n    logger.<span class="fn">exception</span>(<span class="str">"Operation failed"</span>)  <span class="cm"># auto-includes traceback</span></code></pre></div>'

